# Forum: The Market-Model University: Humanities in the Age of Money.

**Authors:** Engell, James, Dangerfield, Anthony

## Abstract
Argues that as higher education has grown, colleges and universities have systematically disinvested in the humanities and developed a culture of credentials. Now market-driven colleges pursue trophies (star faculty, plush facilities, reputation). Academic fields that offer a promise of money, knowledge of money, or a source of money are prized, and the humanities satisfy none of these criteria. (MSE)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ579970

